# NickelHome (libnickelhome.so)
#
# This mod tweaks the Kobo home screen by hiding specific widgets after the
# home view is constructed. It is built on NickelHook and is a sibling of
# NickelMenu (https://pgaskin.net/NickelMenu).
#
# Use KoboRoot.tgz on firmware 4.23.15505+ in the 4.x family, or Kobo.tgz
# on Qt6 firmware 5.18/6.x. Qt6 support is experimental. Never rename packages.
# Missing widgets are left unchanged. The Qt6 plugin requires the Home hook.
#
# Configuration lives in a single file at:
#
#   KOBOeReader/.adds/nickel-home/config
#
# Each line is either blank, a comment (starting with #), or an option in the
# form:
#
#   <key>:<val>
#
# Spaces around fields are ignored. If an option is declared more than once,
# only the first declaration takes effect. A reboot is required for changes to
# take effect.
#
# These options hide elements on the home screen by their internal widget name.
# They are the runtime equivalent of the corresponding kobopatch patches.
#
#   <key>  one of:
#            nhm_enabled                - master switch; set to 0 to leave the home screen
#                                         untouched without uninstalling the mod (default 1)
#            nhm_log                    - set to 1 to write verbose logs to nickel-home.log in
#                                         this folder, for troubleshooting (default 0)
#            hide_home_row1col2_enabled - hides the dynamic slot in the top-right of the home
#                                         screen, next to the book you are currently reading
#                                         (when fewer than 2 books are open). Kobo fills it with
#                                         a collection, author, wishlist, related reads,
#                                         recommendations, or Top Picks / store tile ("Top 50",
#                                         "Coming soon to audiobooks", ...); hiding the slot
#                                         also stops it from being filled, so content arriving
#                                         later (e.g. after a store sync) can't re-show it
#            hide_home_row2col2_enabled - hides the `row2col2` dynamic slot next to "My Books"
#                                         (same kind of content as above, plus the quick tour
#                                         card) and stops it from being filled; this is a
#                                         visual-only hide which disables the widget and makes
#                                         it transparent without collapsing its layout space so
#                                         "My Books" doesn't break
#            hide_home_row2_enabled     - hides both "My Books" and the quick tour card;
#                                         your books should still be accessible via the
#                                         appropriate navigation tab (unless also hidden)
#            hide_home_row3_enabled     - hides the footer row below "My Books" on the home
#                                         screen, which often advertises features like the
#                                         Kobo Store, Pocket, and more
#            hide_home_row2col1_enabled - hides My Books independently (Qt6 only)
#            tolino_home_books_enabled  - uses Kobo's book layout on Tolino (Qt6 only,
#                                         default 0; does not change account state)
#   <val>  0 or 1
#
# Qt6 keeps native content updates and reapplies the hide rules afterwards.
# My Books remains available with one or two books and hides when it has no
# books to show. Store promotions never replace it while the mod is enabled.
# Explicit hide settings still take precedence.
# Neither package adds an interactive Settings page. Edit config and reboot.
# On Qt6 Kobo, the reading prompt opens My Books while the mod is enabled.
#
# Example:
#   hide_home_row1col2_enabled:1
#   hide_home_row2col2_enabled:1
#   hide_home_row2_enabled:0
#   hide_home_row3_enabled:1
#
# NickelHome writes a log to nickel-home.log in this folder. On a healthy boot it stays short:
# the mod version, your firmware version, and which widgets it hid. Attach it to a bug report.
# Set nhm_log:1 for more detail. The file is size-capped and rotates to nickel-home.log.old.
#
# To uninstall NickelHome, delete the `uninstall` file in
# KOBOeReader/.adds/nickel-home/, then reboot. NickelHome treats that file going
# missing as an uninstall request: on the next startup it removes its installed
# library and the whole KOBOeReader/.adds/nickel-home/ folder.
#
# You can also create a new (empty) file named `uninstall-now` in the same
# folder, then reboot, which does the same thing. Deleting the entire folder
# works too. As a last resort, you can trigger the failsafe mechanism by
# immediately powering off the Kobo after it starts booting.
